  "sourceMethod": "Eight independently generated reference paintings were filled from blank 8×4 division guides and their ordered roster, with no prior-release painting used. Each lower-rank sheet is a freshly generated costume, pose and scene edition referencing only the corresponding new U sheet. The exclusive Ieyasu portrait was separately illustrated from a reference depicting him in later life. See the exclusive record for this asset's revision and art direction.",
  "baseInstruction": "Class: historical game character illustration. The flat 8 across, 4 down color guide provided is solely an exact atlas template. Replace each of its 32 rectangular areas with an entirely original, DIFFERENT premium cinematic illustrated character painting from scratch. Canvas must remain exactly 3:2 landscape containing EXACTLY EIGHT equal columns across and FOUR equal rows down. Each cell alone is a full 3:4 portrait. Fill all 32 cells to their edges; adjacent paintings meet directly as straight vertical/horizontal cuts with no frames, no gutters, no margins. Strictly one human HEAD per cell (32 heads total). Center head and upper body at 50% of each cell width, eyes about 37% from top, fully contain silhouettes and leave breathing space above headdresses. Heroic U tier: spectacularly designed individual lacquered Japanese armor or court robes, embroidery and patterned sleeves, sculptural helmets and unique expressive faces, varied poses and deep scene-specific backgrounds. Masterful modern Japanese anime/sumi-e crossover, strong sinuous black outlines, crisp painted facial modeling, open shapes, intentional contrast, rich lapis / vermilion / dark indigo / antique gilding. High-end Character design, natural mature faces, varying ages and facial hair, some handsome young warriors, clever ministers, elderly veterans, ordained monks, women specified. Each panel is a true character close-up from scalp to chest, not tiny people standing in a generic environment. Each officer is an independent character (not 32 costumes of one person); use individualized casting, head silhouette and PERSONALITY based on name. Favors graphic shadow and deliberate rim lighting, intricate period material, real human character without human photography, no generic 3D renders. No letters, writing, seals, ranks, badges, UI, panels within a portrait, or floating particles. Use these EXACT positions. Do not draw or print their names.",
  "tierInstruction": "Use case: identity-preserve. The single input is a just-painted set of 32 DIFFERENT characters in an exact 8 columns ACROSS × 4 rows DOWN gallery. Produce a NEW, separately painted rank edition from this visual reference for a premium Japanese historical collectible game. Redraw each as a new illustration; preserve all 32 people's gender, ages, striking facial features, hair, beard and recognizable face, precise 8×4 deployment, left-to-right row order and no padding. Replace the entire costumes, silhouette, poses, backdrops, props and scene LIGHTING according to the tier art direction below. Keep readable distinct attractive hand-drawn expressiveness within each established cell. Head chest or waist portrait, full head and headdress contained, face centered horizontally around 35-42% of cell height. Clothes individual and appropriate to officer identity, especially monks and women. Respect likeness of each input person, concentrated linework, layered Japanese pigment, rich engraved details, texture in broad shapes. Every cell must show a single person with one head, no other visible people in that cell. Exact same 3:2 total canvas, 32 contiguous borderless 3:4 portrait pictures. Front or 3/4 chests, intentionally varied faces, shoulder and hand pose; never add title, text, signatures, gutters, frames. Do not merely recolor the input: REMOVE the U rank crown/armor ensemble and build new period clothing and contrasting context specifically as follows:",
  "tierDirections": {
    "D": "D · Dawn duties. Intimate portraits in the softly lit plain paper light of daybreak: officers in simple elegant flax, natural undyed indigo linen kosode, robe knot and bamboo or worn-leather fastening, hair tied or covered by a plain band, humble but carefully sculpted silhouettes. Minimal clouded earthen-wash backdrop and warm ochre. Younger expressions but same age/identity. Individual cloth seams, sober and absolutely distinct from gilt splendor. No armor or heavy jewelry.",
    "C": "C · First service. Waist-up people turned toward the light at a post-town gate, half-length utility haori over gathered indigo or jade patterned kosode; close pinned shoulder guards and utilitarian tasuki ties for warriors, modest cropped caps or simple eboshi for courtiers. Bark-brown at morning with carmine rope. Differing silhouettes, change the angle of cloak/shoulder and the direction of gaze. Streamlined restrained everyday clothing, few gold details.",
    "B": "B · Argent field. Individual lamellar cuirasses with cool silvery/steel plate and purple-black cotton, short sleeveless jinbaori, dark plum leather cords; light individual helmets/headbands tied behind, not huge gold antlers. Dynamic ready posture and crisp blue dawn with silk camp screens, mountain slopes, dew/mist. A few scholars hold fan, document, brush; do not reuse their U kit. Rich shoulder redrawing, lean trim.",
    "A": "A · Vermilion banners. Captains at the edge of a windblown autumn fortress, strong three-quarter view as people adjust their gloves/forearm or hold a sash. Deep true red, mars violet and dark indigo lacquer, shadowed carved rising shoulder pauldrons, officer-specific tall kabuto with a clean geometric mae-date, patterned lamellar panels, wind brings hair or silk sleeve to one side. Gold kept to fittings. Text-free individual standard shapes in backdrop, commanding crisp painterly light.",
    "S": "S · Grand procession. Strong upward perspective on majestic individuals in brocade indigo and saffron flank coats, unique armor cuirass with gold chased borders, expressive sleeves and signature military headdress or court cap. Elaborate lacquer toggles and blue-green silk lacing. High diagonals across silhouette, beautiful daylight on detailed faces, blue-and-gold river and celebratory distant branches. Compose each hero's portrait anew around an authentic crafted costume and expansive placid light.",
    "SS": "SS · Palace of night. Weighty indigo blackout silhouettes with brilliantly burnished silver, individually carved black Namban armor or sharply tailored court dress, long black-purple mantles and metallic pauldrons, optional folding fan at hand. Moonlight edge light on cheeks and armor. New slightly turned poses looking over shoulder or down in thought, temple courtyard, abstract night clouds or moonlit windows. Gold appears as small quiet inlay. Ornamental profiles fill the canvas but never obscure the eyes.",
    "SSS": "SSS · Vermilion Phoenix. Visually spectacular prestigious officers in red-lacquer and pale-gold engraved breastplate or heavily woven crimson imperial brocade, dramatic parted battle cloak / fabric billowing upward, fierce serene turn to camera, individually sculpted helmet silhouette, bright aureate light, charcoal shadows. Background abstract brushpainted red-gilt midday cloud and folded screens; avoid costume reuse from U. Rich but clean readable faces against full-bleed imagery. Some intricate motifs consist of clouds, cranes, grasses or ferns without type."
  },
